Chapter: RocIterKeepIf
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: iterator-like keep_if skips rejected tag payloads". A lazy stream
 filtered by a predicate:

     keep_if : Iter(a), (a -> Bool) -> Iter(a)
     keep_if = |iter, pred|
         { next: || match (iter.next)() {
             One({ item, rest }) =>
                 if pred(item) { One({ item, rest: Iter.keep_if(rest, pred) }) }
                 else { (Iter.keep_if(rest, pred).next)() }
             Done => Done } }
     kept = Iter.keep_if(range_to(1, 4), |item| item == 2)

 and Roc expects 2.

 The same two adaptations `roc-iter-map.codex` records -- Codex has no
 nullary function type, so the thunk takes an ignored Integer; and Codex has
 no anonymous record, so `One` carries its two as constructor fields.

 What this asks that `roc-iter-map` does not: the REJECT branch. Where map
 always rebuilds a `One`, keep_if's else-branch builds a fresh iterator and
 immediately enters it -- `((iter-keep-if rest pred).next) 0` -- so the
 recursion goes through a record field of a value that was constructed one
 expression earlier and is never bound. That is a call whose callee is a
 closure the same expression just built, which is the neighbourhood of
 findings 38 and 40.

Section: Types

  Iter (a) = record {
   next : Integer -> Step a
  }

  Step (a) = | One (a) (Iter a) | Done

Section: Functions

  iter-keep-if : Iter a, (a -> Boolean) -> Iter a
  iter-keep-if (it) (pred) =
   Iter { next = \ignored -> when ((it.next) 0)
     is One (item) (rest) -> if pred item then One item (iter-keep-if rest pred)
        else ((iter-keep-if rest pred).next) 0
     is Done -> Done }

  range-to : Integer, Integer -> Iter Integer
  range-to (start) (stop) =
   Iter { next = \ignored -> if start == stop then Done
     else One start (range-to (start + 1) stop) }

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let kept = iter-keep-if (range-to 1 4) (\item -> item == 2)
   in when ((kept.next) 0)
    is One (item) (rest) -> print-line-uni (show item)
    is Done -> print-line-uni (show (0 - 1))
  end
